# Keeps the Docker build context small and fast. mail-mock-server's
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .` from the repo root (it needs every workspace
# member's Cargo.toml present to resolve the lockfile, even though it only
# compiles the mail-mock-server package -- see that Dockerfile's comment),
# so without this, Docker would copy the entire cargo `target/` directory
# (easily multiple
# gigabytes) into the build context on every build.
target/
.git/
tmp/
*.db
